<title>USA: HAWAII COFFEE OUTPUT SEEN AT 30-YEAR HIGH - USDA.</title>
<headline>HAWAII COFFEE OUTPUT SEEN AT 30-YEAR HIGH - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hawaii is expected to produce 6.4 million lbs of coffee in the 1996-97 season, the largest harvest in three decades, U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In its monthly crop report, USDA estimated coffee production increased on the islands of Maui, Molokai, Oahu and Kauai while production on the island of Hawaii fell due to a dry spring.</p>
<p>The state of Hawaii should produce 6.4 million lbs of coffee, up 19 percent from last season and the biggest crop since 8.04 million lbs were harvested in 1966-67, USDA said.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
